+/* Logged-holiday month cell — a real amber fill (matching the same
+   --amber-bg fill used everywhere else in the app for "highlighted in
+   amber": .cell-amber, .st-hold, .pr-medium, .badge-r, .sev-review, …)
+   rather than an inset box-shadow border alone. A box-shadow-only outline
+   on a <td> inside a `border-collapse: collapse` table gets painted under
+   the neighbouring cells' collapsed borders in most browsers, so it read
+   as "basically invisible" even though the class was applied correctly —
+   this is the fix for that. The border is kept as a secondary accent now
+   that the fill makes the cell unmistakably highlighted. */
+td.has-note { background: var(--amber-bg) !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--amber); position: relative; z-index: 1; }
 .legend-dot.note-dot { background: var(--amber); border-radius: 50%; }
 
